  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": null,
      "what": "This study introduces a method for multiscale space-time varying coefficient modeling by extending Generalized Additive Models (GAMs) into the temporal domain. The approach generates multiple competing GAMs with different space-time interaction specifications for each predictor, selecting the optimal model using the Akaike Information Criterion (AIC). When tested on simulated data and an empirical case study, the selected GAM outperformed Multiscale Geographically and Temporally Weighted Regression (MGTWR) in model fit.",
      "why": "It provides a systematic way to determine the exact nature and scale of space-time dependencies in predictor-to-response relationships, relaxing rigid assumptions about how spatial and temporal variations interact."
    }
